<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Madras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1769</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-mysore-war">First Anglo-Mysore War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> was concluded on 4 April 1769 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> and the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-mysore-war">First Anglo-Mysore War</a> after Hyder's cavalry appeared near Madras. Both sides restored their conquests and promised to aid each other if attacked. The Company's failure to help Hyder when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> invaded Mysore in 1771 left lasting distrust.</p></div>
